Henry J Cobb wrote:
> I think it would be fun to have really oddball abilities for various
> gems to give more characters chances to know their type without granting
> an ID that can be cashed in at a store.  (And shouldn't more store types
> accept IDed gems?)
> 
> Tourmaline (add, just about any color): Absorbs one lightining attack
> and is destroyed.

I'm not going to go walking around letting myself get hit by lightning
just to identify gems, nor am I going to slow my search for reflection
any just because I'm carrying a red, yellow, blue, and/or green gem.

> Opal: Carrying one or more adds +1 to IQ for searching only.

I'm not going to spend any time finding and identifying this gem just
for some obscure fractional bonus to searching.

> Diamond: Carrying one or more reduces confusion or hallucination by one
> turn.

Confusion and hallucination last one turn for me, since I carry a
unicorn horn and will most certainly have found one by the time I can
find and identify diamonds.

> Citrine: Each one gives a 5% chance of foiling a money stealing attack.

I carry my money in a bag; all steal attacks fail anyway.

> Emerald: Carrying one or more adds +1 to rolls against drowning.

There are no rolls against drowning.  Either you drown or you don't,
based on specific criteria.  For example: "If an eel grabs you, you have
one turn to save yourself.  Try not to be burdened."

> Amber: Dipped in Poison to convert to Booze.

I'd rather have a potion of sickness so I could poison things; booze is
a far more common randomly generated potion, what with delicatessens/etc
and the possibility of the Gnome King's Cellar.

Overall, also, I'm likely to just dilute them both for more holy water.

> Garnet: Gives a tiny chance of avoiding poison effects.

I'm not going to slow my rapid search in the early game for poison
resistance any just because I'm carrying a gem of
(whatever-color-garnet-is).

> Dilithium Crystal: Consumed in Fusion Sword Hilts.

By the time I can find and identify dilithium crystals, I'm already well
into the process of Just Ascending.

